# Lane M-engine — rig A/B + evidence log (editor + keymap subsystem swap)

Worktree: `.worktrees/lane-engine` (branch `lane/engine`). Scope: dissolve
the K-1..K-9 keymap deltas + swap the composer editing ENGINE by routing
both subsystems onto the opentui-rust ports (`opentui-keymap` engine,
`opentui-core` EditBuffer/EditorView textarea line) as LIBRARIES behind
`OC_ENGINE_OPENTUI` (default OFF until proof; old paths stay one release).

## Design (frozen before implementation)

* **Keymap**: the oc-tui-core `Keymap` facade (mod.rs) + DATA table
  (table.rs) stay byte-identical; the ENGINE beneath becomes an enum
  `EngineSel::{Legacy, Opentui}`. `OpentuiKeymap` (keymap/opentui.rs)
  owns an `opentui_keymap::Keymap` built with `create_default_opentui_
  keymap(OpenTuiHost)` and registers EXACTLY v2's context/keymap.tsx
  Provider set: comma bindings, the enter/esc/pgdown/pgup alias expander,
  base-layout fallback, escape-clears-pending (any escape, K-6),
  backspace-pops-pending (K-7), timed leader (explicit 2000ms — K-4).
  Layers: base = global mode; input/dialog/autocomplete/diff = mode
  gated via the `opencode.mode` data key (set from the facade's mode
  stack top); owned/plugin layers at priority −1 like the legacy path.
  Commands are registered per-layer with sink closures so dispatch
  reports the fired name (the always-accept runner parity).
  `lookup_base` = dispatch with the mode key set to a sentinel no layer
  uses (named-mode layers inert → base-only resolution).
* **Editor**: oc-tui-core gains `text_edit_opentui::TextAreaOpentui` —
  the SAME observable contract as `text_edit::TextArea` (char-offset
  text/caret/anchor mirror, EditCommand surface, EditOutcome deltas)
  backed by `opentui_core::editor::{EditBuffer, EditorView}` with
  WrapMode::Word (TextareaRenderable's default) + the composer inner
  width as the viewport (the same `mount_height` formula, extracted
  shared). Select motions mirror EditBufferRenderable's keyboard
  selection (anchor kept in offset space across moves). Char-offset ↔
  display-width-offset conversions walk the buffer's cluster table.
* Flag: `OC_ENGINE_OPENTUI` (OnceLock at first read; opt-IN while
  unproven — flips default ON after the A/B proof, `=0` keeps legacy
  one release). In-process test override for nextest/libtest parity
  runs of BOTH paths.

## Phase log


## Phase 1 — keymap subsystem swap (COMPLETE, 66/66 green)

* `crates/oc-tui-core/src/keymap/opentui.rs` (NEW, ~560 LOC): the
  `OpentuiKeymap` engine adapter over `opentui_keymap::Keymap`
  (with_clock + createDefaultOpenTuiKeymap's registration set + v2's
  exact Provider addons: comma bindings, the enter/esc/pgdown/pgup
  alias expander, base-layout fallback, escape-clears (any escape),
  backspace-pops, timed leader @ v2's explicit 2000ms).
* `keymap/mod.rs`: facade's engine → `EngineSel::{Legacy, Opentui}`
  (flag-latched at construction); ALL facade signatures unchanged
  (pending_display &self→&mut self — oc-tui call sites all &mut).
* `keymap/parity_tests.rs` (NEW): the resolution parity table — every
  default-table spec (~202) resolves IDENTICALLY on both engines in
  its layer's mode context (kind+command, displays normalized); the
  K-1..K-9 before/after suite; conflict parity (ctrl+d/ctrl+p/down ×
  modes); lookup_base parity; overrides/leader-rebind/owned on the
  opentui rebuild path.

### Findings so far (engine-behavior deltas surfaced BY the swap)

1. **The donor's sequence grammar has NO `>` separator** — parts
   concatenate ("gg") and leader chords are the `<leader>` token form
   ("<leader>e"). The adapter's chord_spec emits the correct grammar.
2. **Pending display**: the opentui engine shows the `<leader>` token
   form (upstream getPendingSequence's display — v2-faithful); legacy
   showed the raw stroke "ctrl+x". Not user-visible in our pump (only
   `is_some()` checks) — parity_key normalizes it.
3. **diff.toggle's "enter" spec was DEAD on legacy** (the pump's Enter
   stroke is "return"; the table's alias spec only fired when fed the
   literal alias). The v2 alias expander (K-7 family) makes it resolve
   on the canonical "return" — a real binding revived by the swap,
   covered by the parity walk's alias branch.
4. `expire()` order matters: the pending getters lazily expire at the
   ENGINE's clock — `had` must be read before the clock sync.

## Phase 2 — editor engine swap (COMPLETE, 688/688 oc-tui both paths)

* `crates/oc-tui-core/src/text_edit_opentui.rs` (NEW, ~900 LOC):
  `TextAreaOpentui` (EditBuffer + EditorView, WrapMode::Word, the
  composer inner width as the wrap viewport) + the `EditCore`
  flag-selected facade. Composer seam: `Composer.edit: EditCore`;
  store's edits map + the resync mirror; app boot/resize feed
  `prompt_text_width` (extracted from mount_height — ONE shared
  formula) into the engines' viewport.
* Editor parity suite (oc-tui-core): motion/selection/edit/undo/
  wide-cluster parity + four upstream-faithful DELTA tests.
* oc-tui 688/688 on the legacy path AND 688/688 under
  `OC_ENGINE_OPENTUI=1` (nextest per-test processes latch the flag).

### Engine-behavior deltas (upstream/v2-faithful, each pinned by a test)

1. **Plain moves over a selection collapse WITHOUT stepping**
   (`collapseSelectionToEdge`) — legacy cleared + moved.
2. **Word boundaries** are the buffer's script-transition rules:
   "fn foo()" alt+f hops [3,7,8] vs legacy [3,6,8].
3. **Line home/end readline jumps**: home at col 0 → previous line's
   end; end at EOL → next line's start (gotoLineHome/End 791-825).
4. **Visual motions follow the WRAP model** (vlines at the composer
   width; boundary affinity keeps the cursor on the last grapheme,
   not past the break's trailing space) — legacy aliased logical.
5. **deleteForward's phantom snapshot** (the ported upstream
   double-snapshot): a no-op delete still stores an undo point.
6. **Undo after an external setText**: history clears (v2 rope.clear_
   history) — legacy kept orphaned snapshots (undo-after-submit).
7. **Pending display**: "<leader>" token form (upstream) vs "ctrl+x".

### Bugs found in MY adapter while pinning parity (fixed)

* `offset_to_char` off-by-one on rows > 0 (the row-break walk).
* `mirror_text` must be a no-op on matching text (the per-keystroke
  bridge was resetting caret+history every op).
* Caret placement after range deletes must rebase in char space.
* The donor key grammar: no ">" separator — `<leader>e` tokens +
  concatenated parts ("gg"); alias expander revive of diff.toggle's
  "enter" spec (it was DEAD on legacy — the pump speaks "return").

