## K-1..K-9 disposition table (the lane's close-out)

| delta | disposition | evidence |
|---|---|---|
| K-1 non-leader sequences never armed | **DISSOLVED** (arms + completes — "gg") | parity_tests::k1 |
| K-2 miss re-evaluated from root | **DISSOLVED** (sequence-miss, unconsumed, no redispatch) | parity_tests::k2 |
| K-3 exact vs continuation priority | **DISSOLVED** (high-layer continuation holds over low-layer exact) | parity_tests::k3 |
| K-4 timed leader 1500 vs 2000 | **DISSOLVED** (v2's explicit 2000 on both engines) | parity_tests::k4 |
| K-5 hyper folding | **DISSOLVED** (hyper a distinct modifier in the canonical order) | parity_tests::k5 |
| K-6 escape-clears bare-only | **DISSOLVED** (the v2 ADDON: any escape clears + consumes) | parity_tests::k6 |
| K-7 backspace-pop / comma / base-layout | **DISSOLVED** (all three addons = v2's Provider set; the alias expander additionally revived the dead diff.toggle "enter" binding) | parity_tests::k7 + the parity table's alias branch |
| K-8 getActiveKeys empty at root | **DISSOLVED** (root lists reachable keys) | parity_tests::k8 |
| K-9 layer order / focus / rejection / preventDefault | NO DELTA (was already consistent; re-pinned on both engines) | parity_tests::k9 + resolution_parity_table |

All nine dissolutions are SUBSYSTEM-semantic (the dispatch engine is
the donor port); no behavior was special-cased.
